  "slug": "cross-power-spectrum-b133",
  "summary": "Six preprints test EFT, halo-model and dark-energy mapping prescriptions against simulations, supporting 21 cm, Lyα, SPHEREx and field-level analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is validating theoretical prescriptions against simulations before applying them to data. Two Lyman-alpha works test EFT descriptions: a minimal tree-level model for 21 cm and Lyα auto- and cross-spectra at z=2.4-4.2, constraining HI and Lyα biases, and a power spectrum plus bispectrum full-shape analysis on AbacusSummit mocks at z=2.5 for DESI. The SPHEREx pair forecasts extragalactic background light cross-correlated with CMB lensing, with the second paper reporting halo-model predictions consistent with lightcone simulations. Two further papers show that N-body runs with constant w can reproduce CPL and general w(z) dark energy at the field level by matching the expansion history, with power spectra agreeing within 0.2% in one case. New here is the combination of line-intensity, forest, lensing and simulation-mapping validation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
